#: inc/customizer/callbacks/about-country.php:183
msgid ""
"Records mention the Gopalas and Mahishapalas believed to have been the "
"earliest rulers with their capital at Matatirtha, the south-west corner of "
"the Kathmandu Valley. From the 7th or 8th Century B.C. the Kirantis are said "
"to have ruled the valley. Their famous King Yalumber is even mentioned in "
"the epic, &lsquo;Mahabharat&rsquo;. Around 300 A.D. the Lichhavis arrived "
"from northern India and overthrew the Kirantis. One of the legacies of the "
"Lichhavis is the Changu Narayan Temple near Bhaktapur, a UNESCO World "
"Heritage Site (Culture), which dates back to the 5th Century. In the early "
"7th Century, Amshuvarma, the first Thakuri king took over the throne from "
"his father-in-law who was a Lichhavi. He married off his daughter Bhrikuti "
"to the famous Tibetan King Tsong Tsen Gampo thus establishing good relations "
"with Tibet. The Lichhavis brought art and architecture to the valley but the "
"golden age of creativity arrived in 1200 A.D with the Mallas."
msgstr ""
"Les archives mentionnent les Gopala et les Mahishapala, considérés comme les "
"premiers souverains, avec leur capitale à Matatirtha, à l'angle sud-ouest de "
"la vallée de Katmandou. Du VIIe ou VIIIe siècle av. J.-C., les Kirati "
"auraient régné sur la vallée. Leur célèbre roi Yalambar est même mentionné "
"dans l'épopée du « Mahabharata ». Vers 300 apr. J.-C., les Licchavi "
"arrivèrent du nord de l'Inde et renversèrent les Kirati. L'un des héritages "
"des Licchavi est le temple de Changu Narayan, près de Bhaktapur, site du "
"patrimoine mondial de l'UNESCO (culture), qui remonte au Ve siècle. Au début "
"du VIIe siècle, Amshuvarma, premier roi Thakuri, prit le trône de son beau-"
"père, un Licchavi. Il maria sa fille Bhrikuti au célèbre roi tibétain "
"Songtsen Gampo, établissant ainsi de bonnes relations avec le Tibet. Les "
"Licchavi apportèrent l'art et l'architecture à la vallée, mais l'âge d'or de "
"la création arriva en 1200 apr. J.-C. avec les Malla."

