#: inc/customizer/callbacks/about-country.php:159
msgid ""
"The Terai region, with width of ranging 26 to 32 km and altitude ranging "
"from 60 -305 m, occupies about 17 percent of total land area of the country. "
"Kechana Kalan, the lowest point of the country with an altitude of 60 m, "
"lies in Jhapa district of the eastern Terai. The southern lowland Terai "
"continues to the Bhabar belt covered with the Char Kose Jhadi forests known "
"for rich wildlife. Further north, the Siwalik zone (700 &ndash; 1,500 m) and "
"the Mahabharat range (1,500 &ndash; 2,700 m) give way to the Duns (valleys), "
"such as Trijuga, Sindhuli, Chitwan, Dang and Surkhet. The Midlands (600 "
"&ndash; 3,500 m), north of the Mahabharat range is where the two beautiful "
"valleys of Kathmandu and Pokhara lie covered in terraced rice fields, and "
"surrounded by forested watersheds."
msgstr ""
"La région du Teraï, large de 26 à 32 km et d'une altitude comprise entre 60 "
"et 305 m, occupe environ 17 % de la superficie totale du pays. Kechana Kalan,"
" le point le plus bas du pays à 60 m d'altitude, se trouve dans le district "
"de Jhapa, dans le Teraï oriental. Le Teraï méridional se prolonge par la "
"ceinture du Bhabar, couverte des forêts de Char Kose Jhadi, réputées pour "
"leur riche faune. Plus au nord, la zone des Siwaliks (700 à 1 500 m) et la "
"chaîne du Mahabharat (1 500 à 2 700 m) cèdent la place aux Duns (vallées), "
"telles que Trijuga, Sindhuli, Chitwan, Dang et Surkhet. Les Midlands (600 à "
"3 500 m), au nord de la chaîne du Mahabharat, abritent les deux magnifiques "
"vallées de Katmandou et Pokhara, couvertes de rizières en terrasses et "
"entourées de bassins versants boisés."

